// blink.zp — Your first hardware program
// Zeros Template — Level 0 (Reskin)
//
// One LED. On. Off. On. Off.
// The "Hello World" of robotics.
//
// Codex Labs LLC — 2026

// ── HARDWARE ─────────────────────────────────

led : act(led, pin: 13)

// ── BLINK ────────────────────────────────────

clock : tick(every: 500ms) -> toggle -> led

// That's it. Three lines.
// clock sends a tick every half second.
// toggle flips between on and off.
// led receives the signal.

// ── TRY THIS ─────────────────────────────────
//
// 1. Change 500ms to 100ms. What happens?
// 2. Change 500ms to 2s. What happens?
// 3. Add a second LED on pin 12:
//      led2 : act(led, pin: 12)
//      clock -> toggle -> {led, led2}
//    Do they blink together?
//
// 4. Make them alternate:
//      clock -> toggle -> led
//      clock -> toggle -> invert -> led2
//    Now one is on while the other is off.
//
// 5. Add a button:
//      button : sense(button, pin: 2)
//      button -> led
//    LED follows the button. No timer needed.
//
// 6. Button controls the speed:
//      button -> gate(pressed) -> speed.faster(50ms)
//      button -> gate(released) -> speed.slower(50ms)
//      clock(speed) -> toggle -> led
